 place of feex(ixm1(ix,iy),iy) (only in this expression, so ti's feix keeps ix1). ixm1 differs from ix-1
 only at ix = ixpt1+1 and ixpt2+1 for iy <= iysptrx (probed per family, AIUE-90 task 1), so only those
 te rows fire. Owner, 2026-10-22 (AIUE-90 Q3): a generic site, detected on the small families and, since
 AIUE-92, on the owner families. dnull_imp2 (nxpt = 2) has it per mesh half: ixpt1(1)+1 and ixpt2(2)+1 for
 iy <= iysptrx1(1) = 30, ixpt2(1)+1 and ixpt1(2)+1 for iy <= iysptrx2(1) = 16; at the cut guard ixlb(2) the
 boundary condition overwrites the te row.

